    {
      "bbox": [
        467.67308210784313,
        273.99639962121216,
        89.6563480392158,
        18.585294823232402
      ],
      "text": "Abstract",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/DEZVYK+CMR12",
        "size": 14.34619998931885
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        113.2223893382353,
        307.24522537878795,
        294.9498782271242,
        14.118494949495016
      ],
      "text": "Recent experiments [J. van Mameren",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/DUYJST+CMR10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        413.7265951797386,
        308.0358472222223,
        40.13399223856209,
        12.53723832070716
      ],
      "text": "et al.",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/IDZQPN+CMTI10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        461.7927475490196,
        307.24522537878795,
        468.26465114379084,
        14.118494949495016
      ],
      "text": "PNAS 106, 18231 (2009)] provide a detailed spatial picture",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/DUYJST+CMR10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        94.95160187908496,
        337.15919034090916,
        835.0962837418301,
        14.118494949495016
      ],
      "text": "of overstretched DNA, showing that under certain conditions the two strands of the double helix separate",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/DUYJST+CMR10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        94.95160187908496,
        367.07186111111116,
        835.0924986111112,
        14.11845612373736
      ],
      "text": "at about 65 pN. It was proposed that this observation rules out the existence of an elongated, hybridized",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/DUYJST+CMR10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        94.95160187908496,
        396.984518939394,
        526.8394585784314,
        14.11845612373736
      ],
      "text": "form of DNA (S-DNA). Here we argue that the S-DNA picture",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/DUYJST+CMR10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        630.0769795751635,
        397.7751407828283,
        13.0746956699345,
        12.537212436868685
      ],
      "text": "is",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/IDZQPN+CMTI10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        651.4328210784314,
        396.984518939394,
        278.62497957516337,
        14.11845612373736
      ],
      "text": "consistent with the observation of",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/DUYJST+CMR10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        94.95160187908496,
        426.8984968434344,
        835.0924986111112,
        14.11845612373736
      ],
      "text": "unpeeling during overstretching. We demonstrate that assuming the existence of S-DNA does not imply",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/DUYJST+CMR10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        94.95160187908496,
        456.8111546717172,
        835.1032343137256,
        14.11845612373736
      ],
      "text": "DNA overstretching to consist of the complete or near-complete conversion of the molecule from B- to S-",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/DUYJST+CMR10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        94.95160187908496,
        486.7251325757576,
        835.1051771241831,
        14.11845612373736
      ],
      "text": "form. Instead, this assumption implies in general a more complex dynamic coexistence of hybridized and",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/DUYJST+CMR10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        94.95160187908496,
        516.6377904040405,
        835.1035357843137,
        14.11845612373736
      ],
      "text": "unhybridized forms of DNA. We argue that such coexistence can rationalize several recent experimental",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/DUYJST+CMR10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        94.95160187908496,
        546.5504611742424,
        103.2747727124183,
        14.11845612373736
      ],
      "text": "observations.",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/DUYJST+CMR10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
